The fast path (an explicit `type` is set) is marked as likely with `__builtin_expect`. The members are read into locals once, so the profile pointer is not reloaded. The checks and return values are unchanged, so behavior is identical. I haven't measured the speed-up, and for a function this small it may be modest.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const auto p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p == NULL, 0))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    const auto idx = profileIndex;
    if (__builtin_expect(idx >= p->numFields, 0))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[idx].type;
}
```